{"name":"Syrah","hex":"#792e35","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Syrah","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of syrah."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Syrah"}],"entries":[{"title":"Syrah","blocks":[{"text":"Syrah, also known as Shiraz, is a dark-skinned grape variety grown throughout the world and used primarily to produce red wine. In 1999, Syrah was found to be the offspring of two obscure grapes from southeastern France, Dureza and Mondeuse Blanche. Syrah should not be confused with Petite Sirah, a cross of Syrah with Peloursin dating from 1880."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Syrah.jpg/330px-Syrah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syrah"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Rhones_Alpes_region_with_Ardeche%2C_Drome%2C_Isere_and_Savoie_highlighted.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Rhones_Alpes_region_with_Ardeche%2C_Drome%2C_Isere_and_Savoie_highlighted.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"The Rhône-Alpes region. Dureza is believed to have originated in the Ardèche (#1) in the southwest and moved east/northeast into Drôme (#2) and Isère (#3). Somewhere in this area, most likely in Isère, the vine crossed with Mondeuse blanche, a variety native to the Savoie region (#4), to produce Syrah.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARhones_Alpes_region_with_Ardeche%2C_Drome%2C_Isere_and_Savoie_highlighted.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Shiraz_Grapes.jpg/500px-Shiraz_Grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Shiraz_Grapes.jpg/1280px-S